  <result type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wastewater. Empresas Publicas de Medellin (EPM) y Empresa de Acueducto y Alcantrillado de BOGOTA (EAAB) optimises their main wastewater treatment plants to reduce energy consumption and improve the water quality of the Bogota River. Also, the two companies increase production of renewable energy from the wastewater sludge and improve the management of their assets to improve the company economy and reduce their carbon emissions.</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="277409" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sludge utilization improved at EPM and EAAB based on evaluation of possible uses. 
Process and energy optimization measures implemented at the key plants of San Fernando, Aguas Claras EPM and Salitre EAAB including reduction of struvite formation and increase of biogas production. 
Primary treatment options evaluated and improved at local outlet points along the river of Bogota EAAB. 
Key technical personnel trained in the methods applied across the topics above. 
Asset management improved at EPM, EAAB and BIOFOS based on shared experiences depends on availability of BIOFOS expert.</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Baseline still needs to be determined"></target>
     <actual value="Stable operation of digestors"></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2025-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-12-31"></period-end>
